# SearXNG search skill — environment overlay (copy to your shell profile or
# export before calling; NEVER commit real credentials to the skill repo).
#
# Instance selection: SEARXNG_PRIMARY replaces the built-in instance list,
# SEARXNG_FALLBACK appends a second instance tried in order. Each instance
# has its own auth ("user:password" directly, or a *_CRED_FILE pointing at
# a file with that format); empty means no auth for that instance.
# Without these variables the skill uses its built-in public chain with the
# shared $SEARXNG_AUTH / ~/.config/opencode/searxng.cred default.
#
# Chain profile: "default" (brave -> google -> mwmbl,searchmysite ->
# braveapi, token-gated) or "gregor" (google -> brave -> braveapi, no free
# tier; school instance).

# --- School setup: Gregor primary (open), claw fallback (Basic Auth) ------
# Gregor serves SearXNG on port 80 without auth, reachable via the VPN IP
# (verified from think: 10.8.0.16 over tun0; 10.50.11.10 is NOT reachable
# from think as it routes via the default gateway, not the VPN).
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY="http://10.8.0.16"
# SEARXNG_PRIMARY_AUTH=""
# SEARXNG_FALLBACK="https://searxng.claw.graf.priv.at"
# SEARXNG_FALLBACK_CRED_FILE="${HOME}/.config/opencode/searxng.cred"
# SEARXNG_CHAIN="gregor"

# --- Defaults (built-in, no overlay needed) --------------------------------
# SEARXNG_CHAIN="default"
